From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:07:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mkfs: drop the K&R re-declaration of `llseek()`

`mkfs.c` carries its own declaration:

    extern offset_t	llseek();

`<unistd.h>` already declares it, and properly:

    extern offset_t llseek(int, offset_t, int);

so the local one is redundant. It is also actively harmful under C23,
where an empty parameter list means "takes no arguments" rather than
"unspecified" -- the two declarations then disagree and every call site
fails:

    mkfs.c:262:17: error: conflicting types for `llseek`;
        have `offset_t(void)`
    mkfs.c:3224:6: error: too many arguments to function `llseek`;
        expected 0, have 3

Delete it and let `<unistd.h>` supply the prototype.

With this, `cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c` compiles clean against a foreign
libc using nothing but the gate's own headers -- no compat shim and no
`-std=` override. `llseek` is left as a link-time symbol, which is the
right place for a foreign host to make up the difference.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5)
---
 usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
index 515ad80100..821aad8ee5 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
@@ -259,7 +259,6 @@
 #include	<sys/dkio.h>
 #include	<sys/asynch.h>
 
-extern offset_t	llseek();
 extern char	*getfullblkname(char *);
 extern long	lrand48();
 
